From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:16:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add gridcraft-aros: the spreadsheet in an Intuition window on
 egui-aros

Problem: the desktop app runs on eframe with wgpu, rfd, arboard and
  craft-print, none of which has an AROS backend, so there is no GridCraft
  window on AROS.
Rationale: the spreadsheet (gridcraft-ui-egui's SheetApp) is driven by the
  shared egui-aros integration (winit's contrib AROS backend, egui-winit,
  a CPU renderer, ASL requesters), as in the WordCraft, PhotoCraft and
  PdfCraft AROS ports; this crate only supplies GridCraft's services (ASL
  open, picture and save requesters with the desktop app's filters and
  save types, the clipboard's text for Paste, links through OpenURL with
  the desktop app's http/https/mailto rule), the settings folder
  (PROGDIR:GridCraftData or GRIDCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR, since AROS has no HOME),
  a log file (GRIDCRAFT_LOG) and a --screenshot option for unattended
  checks. The desktop theme watcher is not started: AROS has no desktop
  theme, and its polling thread would keep the pthread library's exit
  handler waiting.
Not provided, reported as unavailable rather than faked: --control (the
  localhost control server), printing (no printers are offered), HTML on
  the clipboard (copy and paste use plain text), files dropped on the
  window.
Scope: a new workspace member, not a default member; other targets build
  as before. Its egui-aros dependency resolves only through the port's
  build (scripts/gc.py patches the pinned egui-aros in); the Cargo.lock
  entries for it are written into the build copy, not here.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: x86_64 ABIv11 build links with no undefined symbols; runs
  in the port's evidence.
Removal: when GridCraft's desktop app runs on AROS by itself.
